course: dictionary
lesson: 7142
title: Church words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one special subject, such as church or religion. You may not know them, but the words around them give clues. «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit came on the first disciples.» The sentence says Pentecost is a special day, so Pentecostal must be linked to it.
explain: Read the clue words in this sentence: «Pentecostal churches stress the Holy Spirit, lively worship, healing and speaking in tongues.» Stress, lively worship and healing tell you what Pentecostal churches care most about. Pentecostal describes churches that put strong weight on the Holy Spirit.
explain: Now use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the hard word: «a church that puts strong weight on the Holy Spirit» still makes sense in the sentence, so your meaning is probably right. If a sentence stops making sense, try a different meaning.
fact: «Pentecostal» describes churches that put strong weight on the Holy Spirit's gifts, such as healing and lively praise.
fact: A «Pentecostal» is a member of one of these churches.
fact: «Pentecostal» can also mean about the feast of Pentecost.
fact: Speaking in tongues means praying aloud in sounds or in a language the speaker never learned.
fact: Pentecostal churches are among the fastest-growing churches in the world.
exercise: «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit came on the first disciples.» What do Pentecostal churches put strong weight on? | Building castles and towers | Cooking special feast meals | *The Holy Spirit, lively worship and healing | Silence and sitting still
exercise: «Pentecostal churches stress the Holy Spirit, lively worship, healing and speaking in tongues.» What is speaking in tongues? | *Praying aloud in sounds or a language the speaker never learned | Reading silently to yourself | Writing letters to friends | Singing in a school choir
exercise: «Baptists and many Pentecostal churches baptise people old enough to decide, usually by full immersion.» Find and copy one word that means going right under the water. | baptise | decide | *immersion | people
test: «Pentecostal» can also mean about what? | *The feast of Pentecost | A kind of sport | The sea and the waves | A type of cake
test: Which word means a member of a Pentecostal church? | A Quaker | *A Pentecostal | A pastor's helper | A Presbyterian elder
exam: Ella says Pentecostal is just a fancy word for church. Why is she wrong? | Pentecostal means a very old building | Pentecostal means any church in the world | *Pentecostal means one kind of church that stresses the Holy Spirit, lively worship and healing | Pentecostal means a type of music only
